{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791193353,"nonce":"v72sq7u8q1rFucN4PuhJH3kdaDU=","title":"CSS font-size and line-height change what is drawn but not the box the text is measured in","message":"Observed with a throwaway test (removed). A non-wrapping text element with a\nclass whose rule says font-size: 40px:\n\n    no css font-size : layout width 61.0, props.font_size unset\n    css font-size 40 : layout width 61.0, props.font_size 40\n\nSo the text draws about 2.9 times larger and its box stays exactly as wide,\nbecause the box is measured at the size the element was BUILT with. The\nstylesheet pass writes font_size into the node's RenderProps after build,\nand nothing carries it into the text node's measure context. The result is\ntext that overflows its box and overlaps what is next to it.\n\nSame family as cfc7347, which fixed letter-spacing. That fix added\nsync_text_measure_contexts, called at the start of compute_layout, which\npushes RenderProps.letter_spacing into the TextMeasureContext and writes only\non a change. It was kept to letter-spacing on purpose, because the context\nvalue for letter-spacing is always 0.0 today so only elements that set it\nchange. font-size and line-height are different: extending the sync changes\nmeasured sizes for every element a stylesheet gives them to.\n\nWhy it matters more under a CSS-first direction (6f7b001, 7cabafe): when CSS\nis the base layer, CSS font-size on text stops being rare.\n\nWork:\n- Carry font_size and line_height through the same sync. Weight, italic and\n  family are the same shape and should be checked in the same pass.\n- Expect cn to move where a stylesheet sets font-size on text a fluent\n  .size() sized: those boxes were too small for what was drawn. Gate on the\n  cn_demo capture and the full suite, and look at it rather than trusting\n  the suite.\n\nNot verified: how many cn_styles.rs rules set font-size on text, so how\nmuch of cn changes.","files":null}]}